    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The suite is green \u2014 only the `AcceptanceTest` (the two contact-preference cases) exists, and both pass, alongside a full `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change follows the exact pattern already used for the other computed Owner fields (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, etc.), keeping structural impact minimal \u2014 two small, cohesive additions and no growth of any existing method body:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `contactPreference` string property (read-only) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line to `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")\n   ```\n\n`contactPreference` now returns `\"EMAIL\"` when an email is present and `\"PHONE\"` otherwise.",
